{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bts1L2nMpiuaEWVe9CvSiR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation\n2\t\n3\tReplace per-AIR `interpolate_columns_gpu` kernel launches in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched descriptor-array kernel per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 AIRs (at APC 300), issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + H2D column-pointer upload + kernel launch per AIR. Nsys profiling shows 4993 total `interpolate_columns_kernel` launches with only 20ms GPU compute time, indicating that allocation and launch overhead (~60-80ms) dominates the 180ms MLE Rounds span. Batching these into one kernel launch per round using the descriptor-array pattern (proven in batch-stacking-scatter and batch-mle-round-kernels) should reduce this overhead to ~5-10ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012DnErZgkr5B8FMDxVSwvp7","session_id":"d96bd5ad-dc55-4cdf-ae15-7b7ce8dfed52","uuid":"4436c6a5-3530-4865-9f9e-4d1967c12ef3","timestamp":"2026-04-13T09:00:36.748Z"}
