{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011GmxBeXTmnawCUMGxHnQLz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D91goqYdchySC2b7wi56D4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation/plan.md","old_string":"Nsys profiling shows 4993 `interpolate_columns_kernel` launches with only 20ms total GPU compute time. Each of the ~310 per-round launches incurs: (1) a `cudaMallocAsync` for the interpolated output buffer, (2) a `to_device()` H2D copy for column pointers, (3) a `main_ptrs.to_device()` H2D copy for main matrix pointers, (4) a CUDA kernel launch. At ~15μs overhead per call × 4993 calls = ~75ms of pure overhead, which dominates the 180ms span. Additionally, ~5000 `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls add another ~25ms of overhead.","new_string":"Nsys profiling shows 4993 `interpolate_columns_kernel` launches with only 20ms total GPU compute time. Each of the ~310 per-round launches incurs: (1) a `cudaMallocAsync` for the interpolated output buffer, (2) a `to_device()` H2D copy for column pointers, (3) a CUDA kernel launch. At ~15μs overhead per call × 4993 calls = ~75ms of pure overhead, which dominates the 180ms span.\n\nA secondary source of overhead is per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls (~5000 `cudaMallocAsync` + `cudaMemcpyAsync`), adding ~10-15ms. These are NOT batched by this plan because `TraceCtx.main_ptrs_dev` is a `DeviceBuffer<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>>` consumed both as `.as_ptr()` in batch builders and as `&DeviceBuffer` in non-batch fallback paths (`evaluate_mle_constraints_gpu`, `evaluate_mle_interactions_gpu`). Changing the `TraceCtx` type would cascade through all evaluator code. This residual overhead is noted as follow-up work."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1418,"cache_read_input_tokens":12456